 "requirements": "Users belong to tenants (memberships). Docs are tenant-scoped: members of a tenant see, add and change its docs; files are not exposed to users yet, and a row never moves into a tenant the user does not belong to. Nobody deletes. Memberships are read-only to users. A file's size is never negative. The tenants table itself is not exposed to users.",
 "expected_properties": [
  "Docs are only seen, added and changed by members of their tenant.",
  "Files are only seen, added and changed by members of their tenant.",
  "Leaving a tenant never grants access.",
  "Whatever is written to docs can be read back.",
  "Whatever is written to files can be read back.",
  "The application role may only select/insert/update docs and files and select memberships; nothing on tenants.",
  "File sizes stay non-negative.",
  "A member reads the docs of their tenants.",
  "A member reads the files of their tenants.",
  "A member adds a file of non-negative size to their tenant."
 ],
